From f953f4c43d63b28046bdd921ffbbe694f891ed5a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cary Palmer <24235924+professorpalmer@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 13:22:15 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 75/79] cuda: fattn-mma: optional fp32 V accumulation
 (GGML_CUDA_FA_VKQ_F32=1, off by default)

The tensor-core attention kernel keeps the sum of the weighted V rows in fp16
(m16n8k16 with fp16 accumulation; tile<16,8,half2>, 8 columns tile<16,4,half2>).
On Qwen3.8-27B every attention op takes this kernel, the prompt read and also
decode / verify (quantized K/V, GQA > 4). When a head spreads its weight over
thousands of cells, the running fp16 sum drops part of each step: against an
exact fp64 softmax on the same cache rows the output of layer 3 at 245k is 17 %
short (relative error energy 5e-2, 60 times the q4_0 error of the cache).

GGML_CUDA_FA_VKQ_F32=1 selects kernel instances (head sizes 128 and 256, Turing
and newer, no logit softcap) with fp32 V tiles (tile<16,16,float> and
tile<16,8,float>; mma with fp32 accumulation), fp32 rescale loops, and a
write-out of fp16 values to shared memory. The rows of the softmax meta data
keep the fp16 tile layout.

RTX 4070, a 2-bit Qwen3.8-27B quant (measured on this engine):
- op test FLASH_ATTN_EXT against the CPU with the switch on: hsk 256 251/251,
  hsk 128 609/609 pass; test-batch-identity 2 to 33 rows: pass.
- exact softmax against the engine output (a dump of the
  K/V rows at 245k): layer 3 at 245k 5.1e-2 -> 2.3e-6, layer 63 8.1e-3 -> 8.3e-7,
  all layers and depths now 1e-7 to 2e-6.
- KL to the golden-set BF16 reference, 7 long documents, by depth band:
  +0.42 % (0-32k) to +0.86 % (128-256k), all +0.82 %; NLL of the true next
  token: +0.0008 (0-32k), -0.0002 (128-256k, interval includes 0).
- prompt read of that pass: 490 -> 432 tok/s (-12 %).
Not the default: the KL gate failed (the reference most likely sums V in fp16
in the same way) and the read costs 12 %.

(cherry picked from commit 6ac53e5d29e8e591ed28433f289ab2e9ec67f8c0)
